s 57:2\" href=\"/Psalms.57.2\">ψ 57:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 71:18\" href=\"/Psalms.71.18\">71:18</a>; <a data-ref=\"Job 27:5\" href=\"/Job.27.5\">Jb 27:5</a> +; of the <em>past</em> (rare), <a data-ref=\"Exodus 15:16\" href=\"/Exodus.15.16\">Ex 15:16</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עד יעבור עמך</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Exodus 15:16\" href=\"/Exodus.15.16\">16</a> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 10:13\" href=\"/Joshua.10.13\">Jos 10:13</a> (poet.) <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד יִקֹּם גּוֹי אוֹיְבָיו</span>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 73:17\" href=\"/Psalms.73.17\">ψ 73:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 29:34\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.29.34\">2 Ch 29:34</a>. In poetry, <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד</span> is sometimes used to mark not an absolute close, but an epoch, or turning-point, in the fut., as <a data-ref=\"Psalms 110:1\" href=\"/Psalms.110.1\">ψ 110:1</a> (v. De) <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד אָשִׁית אֹיְבֶיךָ הֲדֹם לְרַגְלֶיךָ</span>, <a data-ref=\"Hosea 10:12\" href=\"/Hosea.10.12\">Ho 10:12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Job 14:6\" href=\"/Job.14.6\">Jb 14:6</a> (but v. <strong>3</strong>); after a neg. cl., <a data-ref=\"Genesis 49:10\" href=\"/Genesis.49.10\">Gn 49:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 23:24\" href=\"/Numbers.23.24\">Nu 23:24</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 42:4\" href=\"/Isaiah.42.4\">Is 42:4</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 71:18\" href=\"/Psalms.71.18\">ψ 71:18</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 112:8\" href=\"/Psalms.112.8\">112:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Job 8:21\" href=\"/Job.8.21\">Jb 8:21</a> (but read prob. with Ew Hi Di Du al. <span dir=\"rtl\">עֹד</span> he will <em>yet</em>, etc., understanding v <a data-ref=\"Job 8:20\" href=\"/Job.8.20\">20</a> as present, not future)."}],"num":"b."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>While</em> (rare: cf. <strong>12 b</strong>):—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"with pf., <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:19\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.19\">1 S 14:19</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עד דִּבֶּר שׁאול</span> <em>while</em> Saul spake."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"with impf., <a data-ref=\"Psalms 141:10\" href=\"/Psalms.141.10\">ψ 141:10</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">יַחַד אָנֹכִי עַד אֶעֱבֹר</span> <em>while I</em> at the same time pass by."}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"with ptcp., <a data-ref=\"Job 1:18\" href=\"/Job.1.18\">Jb 1:18</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד זֶה מְדַבֵּר</span> (but read prob. <span dir=\"rtl\">עֹד</span>, as v <a data-ref=\"Job 1:16\" href=\"/Job.1.16\">16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Job 1:17\" href=\"/Job.1.17\">17</a>), <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 7:3\" href=\"/Nehemiah.7.3\">Ne 7:3</a>."}],"num":"c."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">עַד שֶׁ</span>- (without vb.) †<a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 1:12\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.1.12\">Ct 1:12</a>. So <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לֹא</span> <em>while not</em> = <em>ere yet</em> (of past time) †<a data-ref=\"Proverbs 8:26\" href=\"/Proverbs.8.26\">Pr 8:26</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עד לא עשׂה ארץ</span> (so <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לָא</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܥܰܕ ܠܴܐ</span>, often, e.g. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 24:15\" href=\"/Genesis.24.15\">Gn 24:15</a> 𝔗, Mt 1:18); and <span dir=\"rtl\">עד אשׁר לא</span> (of the fut.) †<a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 12:1\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.12.1\">Ec 12:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 12:2\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.12.2\">2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 12:6\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.12.6\">6</a> (cf. Talm. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד דְּלָא</span>, Mishn. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד שֶׁלֹּא</span>)."}],"num":"d."}],"num":"2."},{"senses":[{"definition":"Of degree, <em>to the point that, so that even</em> (rare), <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 47:7\" href=\"/Isaiah.47.7\">Is 47:7</a> Thou saidst, I shall be for ever a lady, <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לֹא שַׂמְתְּ אֵלֶּה עַל לִבֵּךְ</span> <em>to the point that</em> (going so far in thy pride that) thou didst not, etc. (but Hi Che Du al. join <span dir=\"rtl\">גְּבֶרֶת עַד</span> I shall be for ever, a lady <em>perpetually;</em> v. 1. <a data-ref=\"BDB, עַד\" href=\"/BDB,_עַד\", dir=\"rtl\">עַד</a>); <a data-ref=\"Job 14:6\" href=\"/Job.14.6\">Jb 14:6</a> (Di De Bu Du) <em>to the point that</em> he may enjoy, etc., <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 22:14\" href=\"/Isaiah.22.14\">Is 22:14</a> (Du). In <a data-ref=\"Joshua 17:14\" href=\"/Joshua.17.14\">Jos 17:14</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד אֲשֶׂר עַד כֹּה בֵּֽרְכַנִי י׳</span>, read <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל אֲשֶׁר</span> <em>because</em> that (Ges Buhl; cf. Di)."}],"num":"3."}],"num":"II."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לְ</span>, a strengthened from for <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד</span> found chiefly in Ch Ezr, and occurring in most of the above senses. Thus"},{"senses":[{"definition":"of <em>space:</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">עַר לְבוֹא חֲמָת</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 13:5\" href=\"/Joshua.13.5\">Jos 13:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 3:3\" href=\"/Judges.3.3\">Ju 3:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 13:5\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.13.5\">1 Ch 13:5</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">עד ל׳ מִדְבָּ֫רָה</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 5:9\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.5.9\">5:9</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">עד ל׳ מצרים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 26:8\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.26.8\">2 Ch 26:8</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לְמִזְרַח הַנָּ֑יְא</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 4:39\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.4.39\">1 Ch 4:39</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לַמְצָד</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 12:17\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.12.17\">12:17</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לִגְרָר</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 14:12\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.14.12\">2 Ch 14:12</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לַשָּׁמַיִם</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 28:9\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.28.9\">2 Ch 28:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezra 9:6\" href=\"/Ezra.9.6\">Ezr 9:6</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לְמֵרָחוֹק</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 26:15\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.26.15\">2 Ch 26:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezra 3:13\" href=\"/Ezra.3.13\">Ezr 3:13</a>."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"Of <em>time:</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">עד לעולם</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 23:25\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.23.25\">1 Ch 23:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 28:7\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.28.7\">28:7</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עד למנחת הערב</span><a data-ref=\"Ezra 9:4\" href=\"/Ezra.9.4\">Ezr 9:4</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לַדָּבָר הַזֶּה</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 10:14\" href=\"/Ezra.10.14\">Ezr 10:14</a> prob. <em>during</em> (Keil: Ges Be <em>with regard to</em>, strengthened for <span dir=\"rtl\">לְּ</span>); sq. inf. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לַעֲלוֹת הַמִּנְחָה</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 18:29\" href=\"/I_Kings.18.29\">1 K 18:29</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לִכְלוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 28:20\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.28.20\">1 Ch 28:20</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 29:28\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.29.28\">2 Ch 29:28</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לְכַלֵּה</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 24:10\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.24.10\">2 Ch 24:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 31:1\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.31.1\">31:1</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עד להשׁחית</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 26:16\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.26.16\">26:16</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לָמוּת</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 32:24\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.32.24\">32:24</a> (‖ <a data-ref=\"II Kings 20:1\" href=\"/II_Kings.20.1\">2 K 20:1</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">לָמוּת</span> alone); <a data-ref=\"Ezra 10:14\" href=\"/Ezra.10.14\">Ezr 10:14</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עד להשׁיב</span>."}],"num":"2."},{"senses":[{"definition":"Of <em>degree:</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לְמַחֲנֶה גָדוֹל</span> <em>even unto</em> (till there was) a great camp, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 12:23\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.12.23\">1 Ch 12:23</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לְמַ֫עְלָה</span> = <em>exceedingly</em> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 16:12\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.16.12\">2 Ch 16:12</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 17:12\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.17.12\">17:12</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 26:8\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.26.8\">26:8</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לִמְאֹד</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 16:14\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.16.14\">2 Ch 16:14</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לְשִׂמְחָה</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 29:30\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.29.30\">29:30</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לָרֹב</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 31:10\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.31.10\">31:10</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד לְאֵין מַרְפֵּא</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 36:16\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.36.16\">36:16</a>."}],"num":"3."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"III."}]},"rid":"BDB06992","strong_numbers":["5703","5704","5705","5706"],"next_hw":"עֲדֶ֫נָֿה","prev_hw":"עַד³","ordinal":"III.","quotes":[],"GK":["6329","6330","6331"],"TWOT":["1565a","1565b","1565c","2899"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}